WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.429
<v Riley Thompson>Thanks for making time — I know renewal conversations land differently this year given everything from August. I want to start by asking directly: where are your heads at?</v>

00:00:13.129 --> 00:00:30.271
<v Frank Delgado>Honestly, we did look seriously at one alternative. What kept us at the table is that the response after the incident felt genuine, not just damage control — the dedicated channel and the health check have both been used already.</v>

00:00:30.971 --> 00:00:43.829
<v Maria Gomez>The health check earlier this month was actually useful — you flagged a potential capacity issue before it became a problem, which is the opposite of what happened in August.</v>

00:00:44.529 --> 00:01:01.671
<v Riley Thompson>That's great to hear, and exactly the direction we want this relationship to go. Let's talk terms. Given where things stand, would you prefer to lock in another 2-year term, or would a shorter commitment feel more comfortable right now?</v>

00:01:02.371 --> 00:01:13.086
<v Frank Delgado>I'll be honest, I'd rather do a 1-year renewal this time. Not a vote against you specifically, I'd just rather re-evaluate sooner given what happened.</v>

00:01:13.786 --> 00:01:36.071
<v Riley Thompson>That's completely reasonable, and I'd rather earn a 2-year renewal next time than pressure you into one now. For a 1-year term, I can offer a 5% loyalty discount off your current rate, plus we'll formalize the proactive monitoring and quarterly health checks as a written commitment, not just a goodwill gesture.</v>

00:01:36.771 --> 00:01:45.343
<v Maria Gomez>That works for me. I want the monitoring commitment in writing specifically — that's the piece that matters most operationally.</v>

00:01:46.043 --> 00:01:53.329
<v Riley Thompson>Agreed, I'll make sure that's an explicit section in the renewal contract, not just a side conversation.</v>

00:01:54.029 --> 00:02:00.886
<v Frank Delgado>Okay, get us the paperwork and we'll sign for a 1-year renewal at the discounted rate.</v>

00:02:01.586 --> 00:02:13.586
<v Riley Thompson>Will do, I'll have it over by end of week. Thank you both — I know this wasn't a given after August, and I don't take it lightly.</v>

00:02:14.286 --> 00:02:18.143
<v Maria Gomez>We appreciate the follow-through. Let's keep it that way.</v>
